1
00:01:57,942 --> 00:02:01,702
When I was a child, my brother would tell me a bedtime story...

2
00:02:03,052 --> 00:02:05,612
about the man who murdered our father.

3
00:02:07,522 --> 00:02:10,242
Who stabbed him in the back and cut his throat.

4
00:02:10,882 --> 00:02:13,842
Who sat down on the Iron Throne and watched

5
00:02:13,842 --> 00:02:16,152
as his blood poured onto the floor.

6
00:02:17,982 --> 00:02:19,652
He told me other stories as well.

7
00:02:20,712 --> 00:02:23,372
About all the things we would do to that man...

8
00:02:25,252 --> 00:02:28,742
once we took back the Seven Kingdoms and had him in our grasp.

9
00:02:30,842 --> 00:02:33,362
Your sister pledged to send her army north.

10
00:02:34,082 --> 00:02:34,982
She did.

11
00:02:35,432 --> 00:02:36,822
I don't see an army.

12
00:02:37,572 --> 00:02:40,312
I see one man, with one hand.

13
00:02:41,122 --> 00:02:43,112
It appears your sister lied to me.

14
00:02:45,902 --> 00:02:47,402
She lied to me as well.

15
00:02:49,672 --> 00:02:52,582
She never had any intention of sending her army north.

16
00:02:53,162 --> 00:02:57,372
She has Euron Greyjoy's fleet and 20,000 fresh troops.

17
00:02:58,282 --> 00:03:00,352
The Golden Company from Essos,

18
00:03:00,352 --> 00:03:01,752
bought and paid for.

19
00:03:02,122 --> 00:03:03,802
Even if we defeat the dead,

20
00:03:03,812 --> 00:03:06,072
she'll have more than enough to destroy the survivors.

21
00:03:06,072 --> 00:03:06,842
"We"?

22
00:03:08,572 --> 00:03:10,382
I promised to fight for the living.

23
00:03:10,382 --> 00:03:12,232
I intend to keep that promise.

24
00:03:15,072 --> 00:03:16,252
Your Grace, I know my brother--

25
00:03:16,252 --> 00:03:17,652
Like you knew your sister?

26
00:03:20,302 --> 00:03:23,392
He came here alone, knowing full well how he'd be received.

27
00:03:23,662 --> 00:03:27,232
Why would he do that if he weren't telling the truth?

28
00:03:27,372 --> 00:03:29,872
Perhaps he trusts his little brother to defend him,

29
00:03:30,192 --> 00:03:32,622
right up to the moment he slits my throat.

30
00:03:33,712 --> 00:03:35,422
You're right. We can't trust him.

31
00:03:36,722 --> 00:03:38,632
He attacked my father in the streets.

32
00:03:38,632 --> 00:03:41,162
He tried to destroy my house and my family,

33
00:03:41,172 --> 00:03:42,332
the same as he did yours.

34
00:03:42,332 --> 00:03:43,812
Do you want me to apologize?

35
00:03:44,442 --> 00:03:45,312
I won't.

36
00:03:46,352 --> 00:03:47,732
We were at war.

37
00:03:47,892 --> 00:03:50,472
Everything I did, I did for my house and my family.

38
00:03:50,472 --> 00:03:51,692
I'd do it all again.

39
00:03:52,912 --> 00:03:54,562
The things we do for love.

40
00:04:01,892 --> 00:04:04,652
So why have you abandoned your house and family now?

41
00:04:06,972 --> 00:04:09,222
Because this goes beyond loyalty.

42
00:04:12,372 --> 00:04:13,752
This is about survival.

43
00:04:21,342 --> 00:04:23,212
You don't know me well, Your Grace.

44
00:04:25,422 --> 00:04:26,972
But I know Ser Jaime.

45
00:04:27,532 --> 00:04:29,052
He is a man of honor.

46
00:04:30,172 --> 00:04:31,742
I was his captor once.

47
00:04:32,402 --> 00:04:33,962
But when we were both taken prisoner

48
00:04:33,972 --> 00:04:36,972
and the men holding us tried to force themselves on me,

49
00:04:36,972 --> 00:04:38,512
Ser Jaime defended me.

50
00:04:39,722 --> 00:04:41,912
And lost his hand because of it.

51
00:04:44,962 --> 00:04:49,072
Without him, my lady, you would not be alive.

52
00:04:49,432 --> 00:04:52,132
He armed me, armored me,

53
00:04:52,322 --> 00:04:54,542
and sent me to find you and bring you home

54
00:04:55,112 --> 00:04:57,682
because he'd sworn an oath to your mother.

55
00:05:04,302 --> 00:05:05,742
You vouch for him?

56
00:05:08,582 --> 00:05:09,372
I do.

57
00:05:14,742 --> 00:05:16,432
You would fight beside him?

58
00:05:20,422 --> 00:05:21,382
I would.

59
00:05:26,162 --> 00:05:27,892
I trust you with my life.

60
00:05:29,362 --> 00:05:31,012
If you trust him with yours,

61
00:05:31,632 --> 00:05:33,102
we should let him stay.

62
00:05:39,132 --> 00:05:41,362
What does the Warden of the North say about it?

63
00:05:47,272 --> 00:05:49,002
We need every man we can get.

64
00:05:59,062 --> 00:06:00,012
Very well.

65
00:06:21,622 --> 00:06:22,902
Thank you, Your Grace.

66
00:07:01,732 --> 00:07:04,642
Either you knew Cersei was lying and let me believe otherwise,

67
00:07:04,642 --> 00:07:06,012
or you didn't know at all.

68
00:07:06,042 --> 00:07:08,042
Which makes you either a traitor or a fool.

69
00:07:08,042 --> 00:07:10,252
- I was a fool. - Not for the first time.

70
00:07:11,262 --> 00:07:13,202
Cersei still sits on the throne.

71
00:07:13,462 --> 00:07:15,082
If you can't help me take it back,

72
00:07:15,092 --> 00:07:17,102
I'll find another Hand who can.

73
00:07:22,292 --> 00:07:24,462
I suspect one of you will be wearing this

74
00:07:25,362 --> 00:07:26,742
before it's all over.

75
00:07:32,972 --> 00:07:33,892
Coming through.

76
00:08:20,312 --> 00:08:21,782
Don't you have something better to do?

77
00:08:22,232 --> 00:08:23,692
You make my weapon yet?

78
00:08:24,642 --> 00:08:28,452
Just as soon as I'm done making a few thousand of these.

79
00:08:28,652 --> 00:08:30,272
You should make mine first.

80
00:08:30,322 --> 00:08:32,162
And make sure it's stronger than this.

81
00:08:33,752 --> 00:08:34,922
It's strong enough.

82
00:08:39,502 --> 00:08:41,682
It's going to be safer down in the crypt, you know.

83
00:08:43,522 --> 00:08:45,312
Are you going to be down in the crypt?

84
00:08:45,732 --> 00:08:47,712
- No, but-- - But you're a fighter.

85
00:08:49,012 --> 00:08:50,182
I've done my share.

86
00:08:52,192 --> 00:08:53,402
You've fought them?

87
00:08:53,912 --> 00:08:56,032
I did. Some of them.

88
00:08:57,022 --> 00:08:57,852
How many?

89
00:08:58,352 --> 00:08:59,372
A few.

90
00:09:00,912 --> 00:09:01,942
That was enough.

91
00:09:04,882 --> 00:09:05,902
What are they like?

92
00:09:07,472 --> 00:09:08,202
Bad.

93
00:09:10,222 --> 00:09:11,132
Really bad.

94
00:09:11,902 --> 00:09:12,942
"Really bad"?

95
00:09:15,892 --> 00:09:18,932
Even a smith's apprentice can do better than "really bad."

96
00:09:19,752 --> 00:09:21,782
What do they look like? What do they smell like?

97
00:09:21,782 --> 00:09:23,832
How do they move? How hard are they to kill?

98
00:09:23,832 --> 00:09:25,382
Look, I know you want to fight.

99
00:09:25,592 --> 00:09:28,182
And I know you're not scared of rapers or murderers or...

100
00:09:29,132 --> 00:09:30,592
This is different. This is...

101
00:09:31,682 --> 00:09:32,912
This is death.

102
00:09:34,002 --> 00:09:35,192
You want to know what they're like? Death.

103
00:09:35,192 --> 00:09:36,362
That's what they're like.

104
00:09:45,052 --> 00:09:46,132
I know Death.

105
00:09:49,162 --> 00:09:50,702
He's got many faces.

106
00:09:53,772 --> 00:09:55,582
I look forward to seeing this one.

107
00:10:03,432 --> 00:10:05,312
- My weapon? - I'll get right on it.

108
00:10:40,092 --> 00:10:41,702
I'm sorry for what I did to you.

109
00:10:45,742 --> 00:10:47,182
You weren't sorry then.

110
00:10:49,062 --> 00:10:50,872
You were protecting your family.

111
00:10:53,102 --> 00:10:54,752
I'm not that person anymore.

112
00:10:54,972 --> 00:10:56,272
You still would be,

113
00:10:56,612 --> 00:10:58,552
if you hadn't pushed me out of that window.

114
00:10:59,422 --> 00:11:01,482
And I would still be Brandon Stark.

115
00:11:02,932 --> 00:11:05,412
- You're not? - No.

116
00:11:06,052 --> 00:11:07,522
I'm something else now.

117
00:11:09,372 --> 00:11:10,672
You're not angry at me.

118
00:11:12,092 --> 00:11:13,772
I'm not angry at anyone.

119
00:11:14,132 --> 00:11:15,922
Why didn't you tell them?

120
00:11:16,592 --> 00:11:18,432
You won't be able to help us in this fight

121
00:11:18,432 --> 00:11:20,332
if I let them murder you first.

122
00:11:24,972 --> 00:11:26,302
What about afterwards?

123
00:11:27,122 --> 00:11:29,502
How do you know there is an afterwards?

124
00:11:40,532 --> 00:11:41,422
Next up.

125
00:11:47,682 --> 00:11:49,712
Put a marker in the ground!

126
00:11:51,612 --> 00:11:53,662
Bring it up to the wall!

127
00:11:53,962 --> 00:11:55,572
Up to the wall. All right.

128
00:11:56,092 --> 00:11:57,252
- All right. - All right.

129
00:11:59,402 --> 00:12:01,562
Well, here we are.

130
00:12:02,212 --> 00:12:03,912
Yes, here we are.

131
00:12:04,192 --> 00:12:05,192
Together again.

132
00:12:08,982 --> 00:12:10,872
And the masses rejoice.

133
00:12:12,532 --> 00:12:14,222
How do they feel about their new queen?

134
00:12:14,672 --> 00:12:16,292
She's your new queen too.

135
00:12:18,782 --> 00:12:20,002
They remember what happened

136
00:12:20,002 --> 00:12:22,692
the last time Targaryens brought dragons north.

137
00:12:23,582 --> 00:12:26,052
They'll come around once they see Daenerys is different.

138
00:12:26,052 --> 00:12:28,272
And she is? Different?

139
00:12:28,752 --> 00:12:29,652
She is.

140
00:12:30,142 --> 00:12:31,772
- You're sure about her? - I am.

141
00:12:32,562 --> 00:12:34,072
She didn't seem sure about you.

142
00:12:35,012 --> 00:12:36,282
It's hard to blame her.

143
00:12:37,022 --> 00:12:39,062
I made a mistake common to clever people.

144
00:12:39,062 --> 00:12:41,552
I underestimated my opponents.

145
00:12:42,402 --> 00:12:44,812
Cersei told me the pregnancy had changed her.

146
00:12:45,462 --> 00:12:47,382
A chance for you both to start again.

147
00:12:47,382 --> 00:12:48,362
And I believed her.

148
00:12:48,362 --> 00:12:50,222
That stuff can go on the end.

149
00:12:51,272 --> 00:12:53,162
Was she lying about the baby too?

150
00:12:54,692 --> 00:12:56,762
No, that part is real.

151
00:13:00,302 --> 00:13:03,082
She's always been good at using the truth to tell lies.

152
00:13:04,242 --> 00:13:05,832
I wouldn't be too hard on yourself.

153
00:13:05,932 --> 00:13:07,622
She's fooled me more than anybody.

154
00:13:07,642 --> 00:13:09,382
No, he's right there.

155
00:13:10,032 --> 00:13:10,792
What?

156
00:13:11,912 --> 00:13:13,242
She never fooled you.

157
00:13:14,052 --> 00:13:16,252
You always knew exactly what she was,

158
00:13:16,792 --> 00:13:18,232
and you loved her anyway.

159
00:13:29,482 --> 00:13:30,282
So...

160
00:13:31,952 --> 00:13:35,172
we're going to die at Winterfell.

161
00:13:36,962 --> 00:13:38,922
Not the death I would've chosen.

162
00:13:40,662 --> 00:13:42,022
I always pictured myself

163
00:13:42,022 --> 00:13:43,602
dying in my own bed,

164
00:13:44,112 --> 00:13:45,382
the age of 80,

165
00:13:46,072 --> 00:13:47,362
with a belly full of wine and...

166
00:13:47,362 --> 00:13:48,152
- A girl's mouth - A girl's mouth

167
00:13:48,162 --> 00:13:49,742
- around your cock. - around my cock.

168
00:13:55,152 --> 00:13:57,062
At least Cersei won't get to murder me.

169
00:13:57,762 --> 00:13:59,482
I'm sure I'll feel some satisfaction

170
00:13:59,482 --> 00:14:01,012
denying her that pleasure

171
00:14:01,152 --> 00:14:04,092
while I'm being ripped apart by dead men.

172
00:14:07,312 --> 00:14:08,912
Maybe after I'm dead...

173
00:14:10,352 --> 00:14:12,012
I'll march down to King's Landing

174
00:14:12,012 --> 00:14:13,252
and rip her apart.

175
00:14:13,602 --> 00:14:15,752
You will see the Army of the Dead.

176
00:14:26,892 --> 00:14:27,582
Good.

177
00:14:45,412 --> 00:14:47,572
Good. Yes, aim.

178
00:14:50,632 --> 00:14:51,622
Don't rush.

179
00:14:51,902 --> 00:14:53,062
Come forward.

180
00:14:54,972 --> 00:14:55,842
Come on.

181
00:14:55,842 --> 00:14:56,702
Ser Jaime.

182
00:14:56,712 --> 00:14:57,802
Lady Brienne.

183
00:15:06,152 --> 00:15:09,502
- He's come a long way. - He's all right.

184
00:15:09,502 --> 00:15:11,202
One more time. Come on.

185
00:15:11,352 --> 00:15:14,262
- Still has a lot to learn. - I'm sure you'll teach him.

186
00:15:14,262 --> 00:15:15,482
Better, better.

187
00:15:16,112 --> 00:15:17,862
I've been told you're commanding the left flank.

188
00:15:17,862 --> 00:15:18,772
I am.

189
00:15:19,642 --> 00:15:22,002
It's, uh... It's good ground.

190
00:15:22,342 --> 00:15:23,152
It is.

191
00:15:24,252 --> 00:15:27,022
The rise, it should give us some advantage.

192
00:15:27,022 --> 00:15:28,382
If we can keep a tight formation,

193
00:15:28,382 --> 00:15:30,062
we might be able to beat them back.

194
00:15:30,812 --> 00:15:32,562
Yes, I think you're right.

195
00:15:33,062 --> 00:15:34,712
- What are you doing? - What?

196
00:15:34,772 --> 00:15:37,722
- I think you know. - I truly don't.

197
00:15:37,812 --> 00:15:39,682
We have never had a conversation last this long

198
00:15:39,682 --> 00:15:41,722
without you insulting me. Not once.

199
00:15:41,722 --> 00:15:42,782
You want me to insult you?

200
00:15:42,782 --> 00:15:43,932
- No! - Good.

201
00:15:50,842 --> 00:15:52,502
I came to Winterfell because...

202
00:15:58,252 --> 00:16:00,352
I'm not the fighter I used to be.

203
00:16:02,312 --> 00:16:04,632
But I'd be honored to serve under your command,

204
00:16:04,632 --> 00:16:05,652
if you'll have me.

205
00:16:15,432 --> 00:16:16,662
I better get back.

206
00:16:37,982 --> 00:16:39,442
Forgive me, Khaleesi.

207
00:16:41,712 --> 00:16:43,532
Have you done something to offend me?

208
00:16:44,272 --> 00:16:45,272
Many things.

209
00:16:45,462 --> 00:16:47,082
Long ago and long forgiven.

210
00:16:47,782 --> 00:16:49,212
But you did forgive,

211
00:16:50,262 --> 00:16:51,692
despite my failures.

212
00:16:54,672 --> 00:16:57,662
When I heard you'd named Tyrion your Hand,

213
00:16:58,992 --> 00:17:00,292
it broke my heart.

214
00:17:01,252 --> 00:17:02,442
When I named him Hand,

215
00:17:02,442 --> 00:17:04,892
I didn't know if I'd ever see you again.

216
00:17:05,902 --> 00:17:07,472
You made the right choice.

217
00:17:08,162 --> 00:17:10,402
I wasn't under the impression you liked him very much.

218
00:17:10,402 --> 00:17:11,392
I didn't.

219
00:17:12,022 --> 00:17:13,172
His mouth hardly stopped moving

220
00:17:13,172 --> 00:17:14,852
between Volantis and Meereen.

221
00:17:14,852 --> 00:17:16,912
It was all I could do not to throw him in the sea.

222
00:17:21,542 --> 00:17:23,942
But the mind behind all those words...

223
00:17:26,422 --> 00:17:28,032
He's made mistakes.

224
00:17:28,562 --> 00:17:30,042
Serious mistakes.

225
00:17:31,942 --> 00:17:33,032
As have we all.

226
00:17:34,772 --> 00:17:36,172
He owns his

227
00:17:37,242 --> 00:17:38,612
and learns from them.

228
00:17:39,772 --> 00:17:41,692
You're advising me to forgive the man

229
00:17:41,692 --> 00:17:43,292
who stole your position?

230
00:17:44,472 --> 00:17:45,392
I am.

231
00:17:47,032 --> 00:17:48,912
And one other suggestion,

232
00:17:49,142 --> 00:17:50,212
if you'll allow me.

233
00:17:51,722 --> 00:17:54,882
The moment we can get the last infantryman out onto the field,

234
00:17:54,882 --> 00:17:56,462
we should shut the gates.

235
00:17:56,532 --> 00:17:58,282
Keep them open for as long as you can.

236
00:17:58,622 --> 00:18:00,902
There are still people coming in from the countryside.

237
00:18:07,142 --> 00:18:09,622
Lady Sansa, I was hoping we could speak alone.

238
00:18:28,002 --> 00:18:30,542
I thought you and I were on the verge of agreement before.

239
00:18:30,872 --> 00:18:31,912
About Ser Jaime.

240
00:18:34,292 --> 00:18:36,872
Brienne has been loyal to me, always.

241
00:18:37,792 --> 00:18:39,292
I trust her more than anyone.

242
00:18:40,132 --> 00:18:42,592
I wish I could have that kind of faith in my advisors.

243
00:18:44,052 --> 00:18:45,672
Tyrion is a good man.

244
00:18:46,612 --> 00:18:48,762
He was never anything but decent towards me.

245
00:18:49,322 --> 00:18:52,502
I didn't ask him to be my Hand simply because he was good.

246
00:18:53,282 --> 00:18:56,322
I asked him to be my Hand because he was good,

247
00:18:56,532 --> 00:18:58,212
and intelligent,

248
00:18:58,212 --> 00:19:00,532
and ruthless when he had to be.

249
00:19:01,992 --> 00:19:03,892
He never should have trusted Cersei.

250
00:19:04,992 --> 00:19:06,402
You never should have either.

251
00:19:10,602 --> 00:19:12,072
I thought he knew his sister.

252
00:19:14,082 --> 00:19:16,052
Families are complicated.

253
00:19:17,242 --> 00:19:18,702
Ours certainly have been.

254
00:19:21,272 --> 00:19:23,052
A sad thing to have in common.

255
00:19:25,552 --> 00:19:27,332
We have other things in common.

256
00:19:27,782 --> 00:19:29,872
We've both known what it means to lead people

257
00:19:29,872 --> 00:19:32,752
who aren't inclined to accept a woman's rule.

258
00:19:33,322 --> 00:19:35,202
And we've both done a damn good job of it,

259
00:19:35,202 --> 00:19:36,402
from what I can tell.

260
00:19:39,612 --> 00:19:43,772
And yet, I can't help but feel we're at odds with one another.

261
00:19:45,502 --> 00:19:46,472
Why is that?

262
00:19:51,062 --> 00:19:52,122
Your brother.

263
00:19:55,432 --> 00:19:56,992
He loves you, you know that.

264
00:19:58,842 --> 00:19:59,892
That bothers you.

265
00:20:00,782 --> 00:20:02,862
Men do stupid things for women.

266
00:20:03,802 --> 00:20:05,752
They're easily manipulated.

267
00:20:09,142 --> 00:20:11,112
All my life, I've known one goal:

268
00:20:11,902 --> 00:20:13,202
the Iron Throne.

269
00:20:14,302 --> 00:20:16,702
Taking it back from the people who destroyed my family,

270
00:20:16,702 --> 00:20:19,082
and almost destroyed yours.

271
00:20:19,142 --> 00:20:21,482
My war was against them.

272
00:20:23,512 --> 00:20:25,022
Until I met Jon.

273
00:20:27,292 --> 00:20:29,902
Now I'm here, half a world away,

274
00:20:29,922 --> 00:20:32,502
fighting Jon's war alongside him.

275
00:20:33,112 --> 00:20:35,622
Tell me, who manipulated whom?

276
00:20:43,512 --> 00:20:47,492
I should have thanked you the moment you arrived.

277
00:20:48,792 --> 00:20:49,982
That was a mistake.

278
00:20:53,162 --> 00:20:54,902
I'm here because I love your brother...

279
00:20:56,742 --> 00:20:57,922
and I trust him...

280
00:20:59,152 --> 00:21:01,072
and I know he's true to his word.

281
00:21:02,532 --> 00:21:03,872
He's only the second man in my life

282
00:21:03,872 --> 00:21:05,042
I can say that about.

283
00:21:07,282 --> 00:21:08,502
Who was the first?

284
00:21:08,952 --> 00:21:10,232
Someone taller.

285
00:21:15,872 --> 00:21:17,402
And what happens afterwards?

286
00:21:19,522 --> 00:21:22,832
We defeat the dead, we destroy Cersei.

287
00:21:24,042 --> 00:21:25,152
What happens then?

288
00:21:27,072 --> 00:21:28,522
I take the Iron Throne.

289
00:21:31,612 --> 00:21:32,962
What about the North?

290
00:21:34,222 --> 00:21:36,072
It was taken from us,

291
00:21:36,822 --> 00:21:38,222
and we took it back.

292
00:21:38,222 --> 00:21:41,072
And we said we'd never bow to anyone else again.

293
00:21:41,732 --> 00:21:43,252
What about the North?

294
00:21:50,902 --> 00:21:53,442
Apologies, my lady. Your Grace...

295
00:21:53,942 --> 00:21:55,092
What is it?

296
00:22:16,992 --> 00:22:17,822
My queen.

297
00:22:18,802 --> 00:22:19,722
Your sister?

298
00:22:21,092 --> 00:22:22,022
She only has a few ships,

299
00:22:22,022 --> 00:22:23,362
and she couldn't sail them here.

300
00:22:23,892 --> 00:22:26,322
So she's sailing to the Iron Islands instead,

301
00:22:26,882 --> 00:22:28,272
to take them back in your name.

302
00:22:28,762 --> 00:22:30,142
But why aren't you with her?

303
00:22:37,002 --> 00:22:39,122
I want to fight for Winterfell, Lady Sansa...

304
00:22:41,342 --> 00:22:42,512
if you'll have me.

305
00:23:13,512 --> 00:23:15,092
Milord, we're not soldiers.

306
00:23:15,102 --> 00:23:16,082
You are now.

307
00:23:20,692 --> 00:23:23,342
Look, I made it through most of my years

308
00:23:23,342 --> 00:23:25,032
without ever getting near a fight,

309
00:23:25,422 --> 00:23:27,402
but then I survived the Battle of the Bastards.

310
00:23:27,562 --> 00:23:29,142
Right outside these walls.

311
00:23:29,262 --> 00:23:32,092
If I can live through that, you can live through this.

312
00:23:34,462 --> 00:23:36,632
They'll outfit you with weapons at the forge.

313
00:23:37,072 --> 00:23:37,962
Right that way.

314
00:23:40,112 --> 00:23:40,912
Thank you.

315
00:23:43,482 --> 00:23:45,552
When the time comes, you'll be down in the crypts.

316
00:23:45,552 --> 00:23:47,032
They're the safest place to be.

317
00:23:47,262 --> 00:23:48,872
Through that archway right over there.

318
00:23:49,952 --> 00:23:50,762
Thank you.

319
00:23:53,602 --> 00:23:56,132
Hey, hey, who's next, lads?

320
00:23:56,192 --> 00:23:58,222
Thank you, sir. Come back!

321
00:23:59,562 --> 00:24:00,912
Which way should I go?

322
00:24:06,192 --> 00:24:07,392
Which way do you want to go?

323
00:24:08,922 --> 00:24:12,292
All the children will be going below when the time comes.

324
00:24:13,352 --> 00:24:15,402
But both me brothers were soldiers.

325
00:24:17,472 --> 00:24:19,142
I want to fight too.

326
00:24:24,262 --> 00:24:25,562
That's good to hear.

327
00:24:26,522 --> 00:24:28,632
I'm going to be in the crypt with my son,

328
00:24:28,632 --> 00:24:31,812
and I'd feel a lot better with you down there to protect us.

329
00:24:31,812 --> 00:24:33,322
I'm sure a lot of people would.

330
00:24:39,542 --> 00:24:42,062
All right. I'll defend the crypt, then.

331
00:24:52,672 --> 00:24:54,082
Riders coming in!

332
00:25:19,102 --> 00:25:20,142
My little crow.

333
00:25:20,142 --> 00:25:21,492
I thought we'd lost you.

334
00:25:22,452 --> 00:25:23,552
Almost.

335
00:25:28,862 --> 00:25:29,872
Put them in the stables.

336
00:25:33,962 --> 00:25:35,382
How did you find each other?

337
00:25:35,942 --> 00:25:37,452
We met up at the Last Hearth.

338
00:25:37,732 --> 00:25:38,992
The dead got there first.

339
00:25:43,662 --> 00:25:44,572
The Umbers?

340
00:25:45,222 --> 00:25:46,682
Fighting for the Night King now.

341
00:25:48,222 --> 00:25:50,312
We had to travel around them to get here.

342
00:25:51,082 --> 00:25:52,462
Whoever's not here now

343
00:25:53,382 --> 00:25:54,282
is with them.

344
00:25:55,432 --> 00:25:56,482
How long do we have?

345
00:25:57,672 --> 00:25:59,462
Before the sun comes up tomorrow.

346
00:26:06,422 --> 00:26:07,742
The big woman still here?

347
00:26:11,612 --> 00:26:12,422
They're coming.

348
00:26:13,712 --> 00:26:14,442
Next.

349
00:26:14,642 --> 00:26:16,092
We have dragonglass

350
00:26:17,112 --> 00:26:18,572
and Valyrian steel.

351
00:26:23,222 --> 00:26:24,812
But there are too many of them.

352
00:26:26,242 --> 00:26:27,412
Far too many.

353
00:26:29,642 --> 00:26:31,332
Our enemy doesn't tire.

354
00:26:33,592 --> 00:26:34,722
Doesn't stop.

355
00:26:36,322 --> 00:26:37,262
Doesn't feel.

356
00:26:38,972 --> 00:26:41,122
We can't beat them in a straight fight.

357
00:26:41,922 --> 00:26:43,122
So, what can we do?

358
00:26:45,452 --> 00:26:47,972
The Night King made them all. They follow his command.

359
00:26:49,292 --> 00:26:50,452
If he falls...

360
00:26:52,422 --> 00:26:54,172
Getting to him may be our best chance.

361
00:26:54,172 --> 00:26:56,622
If that's true, he'll never expose himself.

362
00:26:57,612 --> 00:26:58,542
Yes, he will.

363
00:27:00,262 --> 00:27:01,622
He'll come for me.

364
00:27:03,422 --> 00:27:07,122
He's tried before, many times, with many Three-Eyed Ravens.

365
00:27:08,012 --> 00:27:08,992
Why?

366
00:27:10,302 --> 00:27:11,372
What does he want?

367
00:27:11,812 --> 00:27:13,152
An endless night.

368
00:27:14,782 --> 00:27:18,152
He wants to erase this world, and I am its memory.

369
00:27:18,972 --> 00:27:20,482
That's what death is, isn't it?

370
00:27:23,002 --> 00:27:23,982
Forgetting.

371
00:27:26,732 --> 00:27:27,892
Being forgotten.

372
00:27:29,092 --> 00:27:30,492
If we forget where we've been

373
00:27:30,492 --> 00:27:31,722
and what we've done,

374
00:27:32,182 --> 00:27:33,422
we're not men anymore.

375
00:27:34,462 --> 00:27:35,582
Just animals.

376
00:27:36,582 --> 00:27:38,302
Your memories don't come from books.

377
00:27:39,432 --> 00:27:41,392
Your stories aren't just stories.

378
00:27:42,442 --> 00:27:43,722
If I wanted to erase the world of men,

379
00:27:43,722 --> 00:27:44,872
I'd start with you.

380
00:27:46,232 --> 00:27:47,372
How will he find you?

381
00:27:47,862 --> 00:27:49,072
His mark is on me.

382
00:27:50,832 --> 00:27:52,392
He always knows where I am.

383
00:27:53,452 --> 00:27:54,512
We'll put you in the crypt,

384
00:27:54,512 --> 00:27:55,882
- where it's safest. - No.

385
00:27:56,792 --> 00:27:58,082
We need to lure him into the open

386
00:27:58,082 --> 00:28:00,052
before his army destroys us all.

387
00:28:00,382 --> 00:28:01,832
I'll wait for him in the Godswood.

388
00:28:02,592 --> 00:28:04,502
You want us to use you as bait?

389
00:28:04,502 --> 00:28:05,812
We're not leaving you alone out there.

390
00:28:05,812 --> 00:28:07,852
He won't be. I'll stay with him.

391
00:28:08,992 --> 00:28:10,182
With the Ironborn.

392
00:28:13,362 --> 00:28:15,012
I took this castle from you.

393
00:28:15,882 --> 00:28:17,142
Let me defend you now.

394
00:28:26,322 --> 00:28:28,952
We'll hold off the rest of them for as long as we can.

395
00:28:29,772 --> 00:28:30,802
When the time comes,

396
00:28:30,802 --> 00:28:32,322
Ser Davos and I will be on the walls,

397
00:28:32,322 --> 00:28:34,122
to give you the signal to light the trench.

398
00:28:34,282 --> 00:28:37,752
Ser Davos is perfectly capable of waving a torch on his own.

399
00:28:38,092 --> 00:28:39,132
You'll be in the crypt.

400
00:28:40,952 --> 00:28:42,302
Your Grace, I have fought before,

401
00:28:42,302 --> 00:28:43,152
I can do it again.

402
00:28:43,152 --> 00:28:45,782
Alongside the men and women risking their lives.

403
00:28:45,782 --> 00:28:47,352
There are thousands of them

404
00:28:47,542 --> 00:28:48,792
and only one of you.

405
00:28:49,512 --> 00:28:50,952
You can't fight as well as they can,

406
00:28:50,952 --> 00:28:53,062
but you can think better than any of them.

407
00:28:53,962 --> 00:28:55,412
You're here because of your mind.

408
00:28:56,202 --> 00:28:57,812
If we survive, I'll need it.

409
00:29:01,432 --> 00:29:03,592
The dragons should give us an edge in the field.

410
00:29:04,182 --> 00:29:06,762
If they're in the field, they're not protecting Bran.

411
00:29:07,572 --> 00:29:08,852
We need to be near him.

412
00:29:09,122 --> 00:29:10,992
Not too near, or the Night King won't come.

413
00:29:11,632 --> 00:29:13,492
But close enough to pursue him when he does.

414
00:29:13,492 --> 00:29:14,962
Dragonfire will stop him?

415
00:29:15,842 --> 00:29:16,782
I don't know.

416
00:29:17,662 --> 00:29:18,982
No one's ever tried.

417
00:29:25,582 --> 00:29:27,212
We're all going to die.

418
00:29:29,732 --> 00:29:31,352
But at least we die together.

419
00:29:35,892 --> 00:29:37,112
Let's get some rest.

420
00:29:46,162 --> 00:29:47,042
Your Grace.

421
00:30:02,552 --> 00:30:03,492
Do you need help?

422
00:30:04,462 --> 00:30:05,172
No.

423
00:30:06,802 --> 00:30:08,312
You've had a strange journey.

424
00:30:09,022 --> 00:30:10,622
Stranger than most.

425
00:30:12,652 --> 00:30:14,222
I'd like to hear about it.

426
00:30:17,342 --> 00:30:18,952
It's a long story.

427
00:30:19,442 --> 00:30:21,412
If only we were trapped in a castle...

428
00:30:22,582 --> 00:30:25,032
in the middle of winter, with nowhere to go.

429
00:30:48,002 --> 00:30:48,762
Hello.

430
00:31:09,192 --> 00:31:11,152
When Daenerys takes her throne...

431
00:31:12,142 --> 00:31:13,872
there will be no place for us here.

432
00:31:15,012 --> 00:31:16,652
I am loyal to my queen.

433
00:31:17,692 --> 00:31:20,372
I will fight for her until her enemies are defeated,

434
00:31:20,952 --> 00:31:24,372
but when the war is over and she has won...

435
00:31:27,482 --> 00:31:29,882
do you want to grow old in this place?

436
00:31:32,802 --> 00:31:35,052
Is there nothing else you want to do,

437
00:31:35,722 --> 00:31:37,212
nothing else you want to see?

438
00:31:39,692 --> 00:31:40,632
Naath.

439
00:31:42,152 --> 00:31:43,852
I'd like to see the beaches again.

440
00:31:46,922 --> 00:31:48,302
Then I will take you there.

441
00:31:49,202 --> 00:31:50,792
My people are peaceful.

442
00:31:52,062 --> 00:31:53,672
We cannot protect ourselves.

443
00:31:54,682 --> 00:31:56,332
My people are not peaceful.

444
00:31:57,632 --> 00:31:58,892
We will protect you.

445
00:32:10,882 --> 00:32:11,632
Yes, sir.

446
00:32:15,812 --> 00:32:16,882
Have you told her yet?

447
00:32:20,712 --> 00:32:21,412
No.

448
00:32:25,362 --> 00:32:26,632
Being careful.

449
00:32:29,962 --> 00:32:31,172
Biding your time.

450
00:32:33,222 --> 00:32:35,352
Waiting for the perfect--

451
00:32:47,342 --> 00:32:49,222
And now our watch begins.

452
00:32:54,012 --> 00:32:55,812
Gilly? Little Sam?

453
00:32:57,782 --> 00:33:00,132
They'll be safe down in the crypt.

454
00:33:02,172 --> 00:33:03,392
If you want to join them...

455
00:33:08,442 --> 00:33:09,442
To protect them.

456
00:33:10,172 --> 00:33:11,812
Everyone seems to forget that I was the first man

457
00:33:11,812 --> 00:33:13,092
to kill a White Walker.

458
00:33:13,242 --> 00:33:15,372
- I've killed Thenns. - Thenn.

459
00:33:15,422 --> 00:33:16,752
I've saved Gilly more than once.

460
00:33:16,752 --> 00:33:19,762
I stole a considerable number of books from the Citadel library,

461
00:33:19,762 --> 00:33:21,492
survived the Fist of the First Men.

462
00:33:22,312 --> 00:33:23,942
You need me out there.

463
00:33:24,752 --> 00:33:27,062
Well, if that's what it's come to, we really are fucked.

464
00:33:27,062 --> 00:33:30,052
Well, calling you "fucked" wouldn't be strictly accurate.

465
00:33:34,192 --> 00:33:35,802
Samwell Tarly.

466
00:33:36,472 --> 00:33:38,522
Slayer of White Walkers.

467
00:33:38,792 --> 00:33:40,182
Lover of Ladies.

468
00:33:41,712 --> 00:33:44,502
As if we needed any more signs the world was ending.

469
00:33:46,572 --> 00:33:48,362
Think back to where we started.

470
00:33:50,842 --> 00:33:54,552
Us, Grenn, Pyp.

471
00:33:55,952 --> 00:33:57,382
Now it's just us three.

472
00:33:58,632 --> 00:34:01,332
Last man left, burn the rest of us.

473
00:34:17,922 --> 00:34:19,382
I wish Father were here.

474
00:34:21,862 --> 00:34:23,792
I would love to see the look on his face

475
00:34:23,792 --> 00:34:25,392
when he realizes his two sons

476
00:34:25,402 --> 00:34:27,862
are about to die defending Winterfell.

477
00:34:32,442 --> 00:34:33,992
That would be something to see.

478
00:34:40,732 --> 00:34:42,772
I remember the first time we were here,

479
00:34:43,922 --> 00:34:45,502
the first time I saw this hall.

480
00:34:46,632 --> 00:34:48,262
You were a golden lion.

481
00:34:49,462 --> 00:34:51,332
I was a drunken whoremonger.

482
00:34:52,242 --> 00:34:53,612
It was all so simple.

483
00:34:54,752 --> 00:34:56,262
It wasn't so simple.

484
00:34:57,062 --> 00:34:58,632
I was sleeping with my sister

485
00:34:58,632 --> 00:35:01,242
and you had one friend in the world

486
00:35:01,542 --> 00:35:03,042
who was sleeping with his sister.

487
00:35:03,172 --> 00:35:05,062
I was speaking in relative terms.

488
00:35:06,962 --> 00:35:09,752
- Do you miss it? - Of course I miss it.

489
00:35:11,202 --> 00:35:13,532
Well, my golden-lion days are done,

490
00:35:13,542 --> 00:35:16,002
but whoremongering is still an option for you.

491
00:35:17,032 --> 00:35:17,932
It's not.

492
00:35:19,722 --> 00:35:21,962
Things would be easier if it were.

493
00:35:25,442 --> 00:35:27,312
The perils of self-betterment.

494
00:35:35,262 --> 00:35:35,992
My lady.

495
00:35:36,392 --> 00:35:38,342
Oh, we didn't mean to interrupt.

496
00:35:38,342 --> 00:35:40,272
We were just looking for somewhere warm to--

497
00:35:40,272 --> 00:35:42,272
To contemplate your imminent death.

498
00:35:42,282 --> 00:35:43,802
You've come to the right place.

499
00:35:44,402 --> 00:35:46,842
You want some of this piss? It's not bad.

500
00:35:47,372 --> 00:35:49,242
- It's not good either. - Thank you, milord.

501
00:35:49,242 --> 00:35:50,732
I don't think that's wise.

502
00:35:51,292 --> 00:35:52,992
The battle might start at any moment.

503
00:35:56,342 --> 00:35:57,472
Half cup.

504
00:35:59,642 --> 00:36:01,872
- And you? - No, thank you.

505
00:36:01,872 --> 00:36:03,412
I should try and get some sleep.

506
00:36:03,412 --> 00:36:06,092
You really think any of us are going to sleep tonight?

507
00:36:07,572 --> 00:36:08,312
Join us.

508
00:36:10,612 --> 00:36:11,382
All right.

509
00:36:12,002 --> 00:36:12,852
Just a bit.

510
00:36:20,222 --> 00:36:21,532
Well, what do we have here?

511
00:36:21,612 --> 00:36:22,932
Ser Davos, join us.

512
00:36:22,932 --> 00:36:24,182
No, none for me, thanks.

513
00:36:24,182 --> 00:36:25,402
Came here for this.

514
00:36:26,962 --> 00:36:30,152
I figured I could wait to die freezing my balls off out there

515
00:36:31,062 --> 00:36:33,362
or wait to die nice and warm in here.

516
00:36:36,872 --> 00:36:39,872
It could be our last night in this world, you know.

517
00:36:41,432 --> 00:36:43,162
Yes, well, I'm glad you're here.

518
00:36:44,542 --> 00:36:46,232
Here fighting with us.

519
00:36:46,232 --> 00:36:48,252
Glad you survived Eastwatch.

520
00:36:48,252 --> 00:36:49,412
Would you like a drink?

521
00:36:50,862 --> 00:36:52,002
Brought my own.

522
00:36:59,242 --> 00:37:01,262
They call you "King Killer."

523
00:37:02,212 --> 00:37:03,972
I'm sure someone does.

524
00:37:04,982 --> 00:37:07,232
They call me "Giantsbane."

525
00:37:08,382 --> 00:37:09,532
Want to know why?

526
00:37:20,262 --> 00:37:22,892
I killed a giant when I was 10.

527
00:37:25,182 --> 00:37:28,432
Then I climbed right into bed with his wife.

528
00:37:30,132 --> 00:37:33,532
When she woke up, you know what she did?

529
00:37:36,952 --> 00:37:40,612
Suckled me at her teat for three months.

530
00:37:41,492 --> 00:37:43,132
Thought I was her baby.

531
00:37:44,252 --> 00:37:46,102
That's how I got so strong.

532
00:37:47,932 --> 00:37:49,362
Giant's milk.

533
00:38:07,842 --> 00:38:09,522
Maybe I will have that drink.

534
00:38:48,612 --> 00:38:49,842
You never used to shut up.

535
00:38:49,842 --> 00:38:52,142
Now you're just sitting there like a mute.

536
00:38:55,572 --> 00:38:56,712
Guess I've changed.

537
00:39:05,232 --> 00:39:06,682
What are you doing up here?

538
00:39:07,602 --> 00:39:08,892
What's it look like?

539
00:39:09,652 --> 00:39:11,962
No, I mean, what are you doing up here?

540
00:39:14,852 --> 00:39:16,162
You joined the Brotherhood.

541
00:39:16,782 --> 00:39:18,142
You went beyond the Wall with Jon.

542
00:39:18,142 --> 00:39:19,592
You're here now. Why?

543
00:39:22,042 --> 00:39:24,482
When was the last time you fought for anyone but yourself?

544
00:39:27,872 --> 00:39:29,502
I fought for you, didn't I?

545
00:39:40,022 --> 00:39:41,562
Oh, for fuck's sake.

546
00:39:42,442 --> 00:39:44,072
May as well be at a bloody wedding.

547
00:39:46,922 --> 00:39:47,762
My lady.

548
00:39:48,522 --> 00:39:49,792
It's good to see you again.

549
